<Base title="About — Sharad Adhikari" description="About Sharad Adhikari and the work collected on sharad.fr.">
  <article>
    <p class="back"><a href="/">← home</a></p>
    <header>
      <h1>About</h1>
      <p class="lede">I build products where data, design, and practical usefulness meet.</p>
    </header>

    <p>I'm Sharad, currently based in Lyon, France. This site is the public home for the products and experiments I take from an early idea to something people can actually use.</p>

    <h2>What I work on</h2>
    <p>My current work explores real-world data, clear interfaces, and AI-assisted product development. BasketMap is the first project published here: a grocery comparison tool built around real price observations and explicit data limitations.</p>

    <h2>What I care about</h2>
    <p>I care about products that explain themselves, evidence that can be traced, and design that makes the next step obvious. I would rather show an honest gap than hide it behind a convincing demo.</p>

    <h2>Elsewhere</h2>
    <p>The code for public projects lives on <a href="https://github.com/shar107">GitHub</a>. New work and longer build notes will be added here as they are ready.</p>

  </article>
  <Footer />
</Base>
